From b7ec4cf9cd448f68e9ddc10d01e93a92a7177b63
Subject: web: add WindowExtWebSys::set_render_scale
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/winit/commit/b7ec4cf9cd448f68e9ddc10d01e93a92a7177b63
Date: 2026-10-22T08:02:01-03:00

Draws the canvas at a share of its device pixels, which the browser stretches
to fill it. The canvas's scale factor becomes devicePixelRatio x render_scale,
so the logical size stays the same and a change runs the existing scale path:
ScaleFactorChanged, then Resized, as a browser zoom does.

- The size still comes from devicePixelContentBoxSize where supported, scaled
  by render_scale, so the exact measurement is kept.
- The media query keeps watching the raw devicePixelRatio, so a zoom or a move
  to another screen still updates the scale factor under the render scale.
- Pointer positions and wheel pixel deltas use the canvas's scale factor;
  DeviceEvents keep devicePixelRatio, so mouse-look speed doesn't change.
- On a worker-hosted window the call is dispatched to the page like the other
  window setters.
---
